  "finalText": "I built the kinetic typography piece on a 1080×1080 comp, now 10 s (I extended it from 8 s so each phrase has time to be read). Critique scores it 97/100.\n\nThe sequence, each phrase transitioning into the next:\n\n1. **Design is not just**: off-white, words slide in one by one, then the line rises out.\n2. **what it looks like.**: mid-grey, slides in on the same spot as the previous line leaves.\n3. **Design is**: off-white, same handover.\n4. **how it works.**: the payoff, about 1.5× the size and weight, in orange (#FF4A1C), with a spring entrance. Its words slide in, then an orange rule wipes in under it with a small overshoot.\n5. **— Steve Jobs**: small grey attribution fades in last, at 8.6 s.\n\nLayers are named `q1`–`q6` (the rule is `q5`). The phrases are all text layers, with per-word animation and their own exit timing. Those exit timings were retimed so each phrase holds long enough to read.\n\nTwo things you may want to change: there is a short blank beat between phrases (about 0.2 s), so the handover reads as a clean cut-and-rise rather than a continuous roll, and the duration is 10 s rather than the 8 s in the editor's starting state."
